WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:06.940
We're living in a very unusual timeline.
My friend's stock car racing league, NASCAR,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:14.280
has banned the Confederate flag at all events
and properties, period, while the president

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:20.369
of the United States on the same day a rich
guy raised in New York City is loudly defending

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:26.329
Confederate named military bases in the United
States. Says he will not change the names

00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:33.880
of those bases and is being called the Confederacy
second president by a Republican group.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:39.320
So especially for our viewers outside the
U.S., but also for people in the United States,

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.720
just as a sort of refresher, the Confederate
flag was the flag of the Confederacy in the

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:50.110
American Civil War. You had the Union versus
the Confederacy. Some called it North versus

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:56.690
South, the Confederacy fighting for slavery.
Sometimes they say they were fighting for

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:02.590
states rights, too, which I always like to
say states rights to continue having legal

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:08.429
slavery, whereas the union was fighting to
abolish slavery. Of course, the union won

00:01:08.429 --> 00:01:13.780
and slavery was abolished. And the effects
of slavery, of course, took much longer than

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:18.920
just that war to actually deal with. But there
are parts of this country where Confederate

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:25.329
flags are sometimes also called the rebel
flag. They are revered or fetishized in some

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:30.459
way, even in the sort of hill towns in western
Massachusetts where I went near, where I went

00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:35.789
to high school. You would have places just
10 or 15 miles out of North Hampton, Massachusetts,

00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:40.330
which was a super liberal little city that,
you know, the guys thought it was cool to

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:46.030
drive into the vocational school with a pickup
truck that bore a Confederate flag on the

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:54.899
back. And there are those who I believe rightly
see it as a symbol of hatred and oppression.

00:01:54.899 --> 00:02:01.640
And there are others who say it is a symbol
of history and heritage. But in any case,

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:07.490
it is widely now in popular culture being
eliminated. And I quite frankly, I believe

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:12.430
that it should be. I mean, would we apply,
you know, look at the losers in other conflicts,

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:17.260
losers that are fortunately losers because
they wanted horrible things like could we

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:23.290
say that displaying Nazi flags just because
they lost is just it's history.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.720
Like there was a German military and it's
just wrecking like, okay, guys. It's an extreme

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:33.170
example, but I find it to be in very, very
poor taste. Now, this gets us to NASCAR. NASCAR

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:38.880
in the United States is not known for being
made up of the most progressive people. Now,

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:45.030
I'm not saying NASCAR fans are all racists,
but it's certainly a sport that leans more

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:49.630
conservative in terms of its fan base.
And it's one of the few places where Donald

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:53.541
Trump can actually get himself a crowd that
cheers instead of a crowd that boos. And it

00:02:53.541 --> 00:02:59.340
is a place where, unfortunately, Confederate
flags are certainly more common than in other

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.060
sports. You don't tend to see Confederate
flags at NBA Games. You don't tend to see

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.800
Confederate flags at Major League Soccer matches.
And as far as I know, they wouldn't even be

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:12.940
allowed in. To be perfectly frank. But you
do see them at NASCAR races. Until now, NASCAR

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:18.900
has now banned the display of the Confederate
flag at all events and properties.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:25.170
And notably, NASCAR also removed its rule
that says racing team members have to stand

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.790
for the national anthem. And we've seen a
number of sports leagues now say, you know,

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:33.210
if you don't want to stand, you actually don't
have to stand. So every indication here is

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:37.870
NASCAR sees what's happening nationally since
the killing of George Floyd. Bubba Wallace,

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:43.220
one of their racers, has been very supportive
of drivers. I think they're called has been

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:50.900
shows what I know has been very supportive
of the protests. And they are making a decision

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:57.319
that there is going to be no more Confederate
stuff at their races. Now, is it because.

00:03:57.319 --> 00:04:02.060
Everybody involved morally believes that there
shouldn't be Confederate flags.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:07.490
I don't know. Certainly they've made the business
decision that there will be no more Confederate

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:14.569
flags there. Not everybody's happy. NASCAR
truck series driver Ray Cicarelli Cicarelli

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:18.450
wrote on his Facebook page he's going to quit
after this season because Confederate flags

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.630
have been banned. Have fun, buddy. Don't let
the door hit you on the way out. And then

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:29.250
here's the real amazing contrast. Look at
the last 24 hours in NASCAR. And compare that

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:34.460
to the last 24 hours of Trump. Trump putting
out a statement and tweeting that he will

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:40.710
not change the names of Confederacy themed
military bases, saying, quote, It has been

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:46.050
suggested that we should rename as many as
10 of our legendary military bases, such as

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:52.460
Fort Bragg in North Carolina, Fort Hood in
Texas, Fort Benning and Georgia. These monumental

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:58.610
and very powerful bases have become part of
a great American heritage and a history of

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:03.870
winning victory and freedom. The United States
of America trained and deployed. These are

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:11.550
our heroes on these hallowed grounds and won
two world wars. Therefore, my administration

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:17.800
will not even consider the renaming of these
magnificent and fabled military installations.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:23.000
Our history as the greatest nation in the
world will not be tampered with respect our

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:29.790
military. Now, what's funny about respect
our military is that remember the union won

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:35.690
the civil war, meaning that the military should
be respected. The military that should be

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:41.311
respected is the military that fought against
the Confederacy. Because we won. The union

00:05:41.311 --> 00:05:49.880
won. So when you name the four, it's after
the side that lost that was killing the precursor

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:55.580
to our correct military. The Confederacy that
fought for slavery doesn't really make a lot

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:01.121
of sense because you've named Fort's after
people who were against our military. They

00:06:01.121 --> 00:06:07.669
did not respect our military. So, listen,
this is not the biggest issue. I don't really

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:11.260
care what the forts are called, although it
doesn't make a lot of sense to me that we

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:16.919
name them after the losers who wanted to keep
slaves, but who would have guessed, as Barack

00:06:16.919 --> 00:06:22.919
Obama was leaving office, that during the
subsequent presidential term, NASCAR would

00:06:22.919 --> 00:06:27.669
take the more progressive stance of banning
the Confederate flag compared to the president

00:06:27.669 --> 00:06:34.121
who defends Confederacy era statues, figures,
heroes, whatever they like to call them. Republican

00:06:34.121 --> 00:06:38.150
group. The Lincoln Project, which is a Republican
group that opposes Trump, has now come out

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:43.669
and said Trump is the Confederacy's second
president. This is a Republican group which

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:48.440
put out a statement where they said, We never
imagined when we named our initiative to defeat

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:54.460
the reelection of Trump, the Lincoln Project,
that the president would go as far as honoring

00:06:54.460 --> 00:07:00.080
the Confederate generals who fought against
the United States to preserve slavery and

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.940
uphold white supremacy, for all intents and
purposes. Trump today became the Confederacy's

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:13.150
second president. We cannot allow this. And
then they go on to say we need help from Republicans

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:19.979
to remove Donald Trump in November. Strange
times, but I believe the decision by NASCAR

00:07:19.979 --> 00:07:24.740
is the correct one. Whatever their reasons
for doing it. And it's probably a mix of understanding

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:31.240
the way society is going, combined with the
fact that it's probably a a bad PR move to

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:34.539
continue having these flags displayed.
They did ultimately come to the right decision.

